# Registers every pragma-Singleton file below as a globally-referenceable
# type name. Any .qml file that `import`s this directory (directly, or via
# a subdirectory import like "../") can then write e.g. `Theme.background`
# from anywhere, with no per-use instantiation — QML creates exactly one
# instance the first time it's touched and hands that same instance back
# every time after.
#
# Plain (non-singleton) component folders — modules/, components/,
# popups/, windows/ — don't need a qmldir at all: importing a directory
# with no qmldir still exposes every .qml file in it as a type, named
# after the file. qmldir is only required to declare something `singleton`.

singleton Theme       theme/Theme.qml
singleton Metrics     theme/Metrics.qml
singleton ShellState  state/ShellState.qml
singleton Popups      state/Popups.qml
singleton IpcManager  state/IpcManager.qml
singleton ClockService services/ClockService.qml
singleton NotificationService services/NotificationService.qml
singleton NetworkStatusService services/NetworkStatusService.qml
singleton BluetoothStatusService services/BluetoothStatusService.qml
singleton TodoService services/TodoService.qml
singleton MprisService services/MprisService.qml
singleton CavaService services/CavaService.qml
singleton VolumeService services/VolumeService.qml
singleton SysStatsService services/SysStatsService.qml
